# Close-loop

Every turn (local Cursor and Grok handoff into this kitchen):

- If the human corrected you, a check failed, or you used the same workaround again: `node scripts/close-loop.mjs record --source local --workspace <slug> --smell <slug> --evidence <text>`
- If `node scripts/close-loop.mjs status` shows a REPEAT: encode it into lint / CI / hook / Feature Map this turn, then `node scripts/close-loop.mjs encode --workspace <slug> --smell <slug> --evidence <text>`. Do not write another reminder.
- If nothing happened: do not invent a smell. You may say `close-loop: clean`.
- Do not encode taste, spend, merge rights, or Slack secrets.
- Friday encode-lessons is backup. Same ledger (`audit/smells.tsv`).
